WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.518
Treating energy as a resource means recognizing that practical capacity is limited.

00:00:04.518 --> 00:00:07.095
Energy affects attention, effort, judgment, emotional control,

00:00:07.095 --> 00:00:11.144
and the ability to keep acting consistently when work becomes difficult.

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:16.666
A person may have hours available and still lack the usable capacity for deep troubleshooting,

00:00:16.666 --> 00:00:19.243
careful writing, patient caregiving, creative problem solving,

00:00:19.243 --> 00:00:21.084
or calm leadership under pressure.

00:00:21.084 --> 00:00:24.029
Energy is different from time, motivation, and discipline.

00:00:24.029 --> 00:00:25.502
Time is the container.

00:00:25.502 --> 00:00:30.287
Energy is part of what determines what can realistically happen inside that container.

00:00:30.287 --> 00:00:33.969
Motivation can help someone start, and discipline can support follow-through,

00:00:33.969 --> 00:00:36.178
but neither one makes capacity infinite.

00:00:36.178 --> 00:00:37.650
When plans ignore energy,

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:42.068
they often turn normal limits into a false story about personal weakness.

00:00:42.068 --> 00:00:45.381
An open calendar does not automatically mean useful capacity.

00:00:45.381 --> 00:00:49.799
A two-hour block after a conflict-heavy meeting may not support the same

00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:53.112
work as a protected morning block after real recovery.

00:00:53.112 --> 00:00:55.321
Technical work, learning, leadership, caregiving, creativity,

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:58.634
and operations all draw from different forms of capacity.

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:00.107
Some tasks require analysis.

00:01:00.107 --> 00:01:01.211
Some require patience.

00:01:01.211 --> 00:01:02.684
Some require social presence.

00:01:02.684 --> 00:01:04.524
Some require sustained physical effort.

00:01:04.524 --> 00:01:07.101
This course uses a practical, non-clinical frame.

00:01:07.101 --> 00:01:11.887
It is not medical advice, treatment guidance, or a replacement for qualified support.

00:01:11.887 --> 00:01:17.041
The goal is to manage energy as a system rather than a character test.

00:01:17.041 --> 00:01:21.090
Better energy management means matching work to capacity, reducing unnecessary drains,

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:25.140
protecting recovery, and designing routines that make sustainable execution more likely.
